(1624874, 218610, 27812, '<td valign="top">coming back for comments. This is a typical ''outside the box, creative shot'' which unfortunately, will not score well on DPC. Brave entry or not so smart? Brave is my guess. Okay, the pic; Always as a rule of thumb, make your back object the one that suffers from poor vision, ie being out of focus. Not the front one. Selective desat works well hereand looks almost like it could be natural, a great skill and a very good touch. Does it meet the challenge? Well I must admit agains all odds that I think it works quite well, why, and I guess the guess of predictor, this will not do well is because there are plent of simple minded evaluators who want to see a human and insists on a musical instrument. But the voice, man''s most natural and the greatest asset, the voice, comes in a box you can not see... the voice box. And who has a more smoothing voice than a bird or an animal or evenind at dawn, nature itself? Where, if you live in a city has not yearned to hear the voice of silence? Yip, it fits very well. Well captured!</td>', 'coming back for comments. This is a typical ''outside the box, creative shot'' which unfortunately, will not score well on DPC. Brave entry or not so smart? Brave is my guess. Okay, the pic; Always as a rule of thumb, make your back object the one that suffers from poor vision, ie being out of focus. Not the front one. Selective desat works well hereand looks almost like it could be natural, a great skill and a very good touch. Does it meet the challenge? Well I must admit agains all odds that I think it works quite well, why, and I guess the guess of predictor, this will not do well is because there are plent of simple minded evaluators who want to see a human and insists on a musical instrument. But the voice, man''s most natural and the greatest asset, the voice, comes in a box you can not see... the voice box. And who has a more smoothing voice than a bird or an animal or evenind at dawn, nature itself? Where, if you live in a city has not yearned to hear the voice of silence? Yip, it fits very well. Well captured!', '2005-08-19 21:39:20.000000', NULL, 1),
