(1640884, 217967, 2022, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a well deserved ribbon !</td>', 'Congratulations on a well deserved ribbon !', '2005-08-24 15:39:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1641161, 217256, 38648, '<td valign="top">Like the rest have said, great caprure.  I do notice a slight halo around the bufallo, like your editing / blur tool was not zoomed / feathered in close enough.   Trim up a few loose pixels around the bottom of the beast, and improve the blur feature close-in and you''re there.  All in all a fantastic shot.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-24 15:48:41.</i></td>', 'Like the rest have said, great caprure.  I do notice a slight halo around the bufallo, like your editing / blur tool was not zoomed / feathered in close enough.   Trim up a few loose pixels around the bottom of the beast, and improve the blur feature close-in and you''re there.  All in all a fantastic shot.', '2005-08-24 16:47:41.000000', '2005-08-24 16:48:41.000000', 0),
(1641633, 219020, 39038, '<td valign="top">Thank guys for your comments! <br/> <br/>As for the shot itself. It is not a portrait photo. Although I''d wish to. It is a street candid shot. this girl did not know I was shooting at her at the moment. <br/> <br/>I am still new to photography (3 months). I am sucking everything I could about photography. Some of you have given me very good critiques that I badly needed. Here I have to thank BobsterLobster for his helpful critiques. Next time, I should be able to do better. :)<br/> <br/>Thank you all for the votes and comments, again!<br/> <br/>Happy photography!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-24 17:38:23.</i></td>', 'Thank guys for your comments!  As for the shot itself. It is not a portrait photo. Although I''d wish to. It is a street candid shot. this girl did not know I was shooting at her at the moment.  I am still new to photography (3 months). I am sucking everything I could about photography. Some of you have given me very good critiques that I badly needed. Here I have to thank BobsterLobster for his helpful critiques. Next time, I should be able to do better. :) Thank you all for the votes and comments, again! Happy photography!', '2005-08-24 18:34:07.000000', '2005-08-24 18:38:23.000000', 0),
