(1939790, 218667, 44597, '<td valign="top">It is a shame they do not hear or have not heard the music of the V8''s.  Just came back from Phillip Island after watching the final series and it was fantastic.   Good photo, what setting and distance were you at.   Thinking of buying the same lens for my 20D.  Good luck.</td>', 'It is a shame they do not hear or have not heard the music of the V8''s.  Just came back from Phillip Island after watching the final series and it was fantastic.   Good photo, what setting and distance were you at.   Thinking of buying the same lens for my 20D.  Good luck.', '2005-12-10 04:20:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1941876, 218464, 37544, '<td valign="top">This picture is so good. I don''t know why I didn''t comment during the challenge? I gave it a 10. Maybe because I just couldn''t put the words together at the time. I love everything about this photo. The colors, the setting, those jeans, her hair....everything is perfect. Just wonderful. These are the type of pictures I want to take. I love your work.</td>', 'This picture is so good. I don''t know why I didn''t comment during the challenge? I gave it a 10. Maybe because I just couldn''t put the words together at the time. I love everything about this photo. The colors, the setting, those jeans, her hair....everything is perfect. Just wonderful. These are the type of pictures I want to take. I love your work.', '2005-12-11 10:27:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2090377, 218324, 8367, '<td valign="top">This is excellent!</td>', 'This is excellent!', '2006-01-26 23:05:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2094849, 217867, 2553, '<td valign="top">Nice shot!  I like the look of the gold, but if you wanted to try to make it more silver you could try this:<br/>1. Make a duplicate layer.<br/>2. Apply a deep blue photo filter to the layer (Image;Adjustments;Photo Filters. Adjust to the desired opacity (Around 40% makes it silvery)<br/>3. Click on the layer mask at the bottom of the layers palette.<br/>4. Select the brush tool, with black as your foreground color,make sure your opacity for the brush is 100%,(make sure  to click on the little mask icon that is to the right of the duplicate layer icon to make sure it is selected), and begin to paint over her face, and you will see the warm tones come back to her skin.  If you happen to paint over the flute, just switch the foreground color to white, and paint over the mistake- it will bring back the blue color filter.<br/> <br/>Something to try anyway, you may find it useful.<br/> <br/>Again, lovely image!</td>', 'Nice shot!  I like the look of the gold, but if you wanted to try to make it more silver you could try this:1. Make a duplicate layer.2. Apply a deep blue photo filter to the layer (Image;Adjustments;Photo Filters. Adjust to the desired opacity (Around 40% makes it silvery)3. Click on the layer mask at the bottom of the layers palette.4. Select the brush tool, with black as your foreground color,make sure your opacity for the brush is 100%,(make sure  to click on the little mask icon that is to the right of the duplicate layer icon to make sure it is selected), and begin to paint over her face, and you will see the warm tones come back to her skin.  If you happen to paint over the flute, just switch the foreground color to white, and paint over the mistake- it will bring back the blue color filter. Something to try anyway, you may find it useful. Again, lovely image!', '2006-01-28 09:24:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2099329, 218891, 27763, '<td valign="top">Love it!</td>', 'Love it!', '2006-01-29 20:01:14.000000', NULL, 0),
